{"id":"war","name":"War","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:war","torrey:war"],"groups":["Figurative","Warfare of saints","Is against","To be carried on","Armor for","In Heaven"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"War","text":"The Israelites had to take possession of the Promised Land by conquest. They had to engage in a long and bloody war before the Canaanitish tribes were finally subdued. Except in the case of Jericho and Ai, the war did not become aggressive till after the death of Joshua. Till then the attack was always first made by the Canaanites. Now the measure of the iniquity of the Canaanites was full, and Israel was employed by God to sweep them away from off the face of the earth. In entering on this new stage of the war, the tribe of Judah, according to divine direction, took the lead. In the days of Saul and David the people of Israel engaged in many wars with the nations around, and after the division of the kingdom into two they often warred with each other. They had to defend themselves also against the inroads of the Egyptians, the Assyrians, and the Babylonians. The whole history of Israel …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H2719","lemma":"חֶרֶב","xlit":"chereb","gloss":"drought","kjv":"axe, dagger, knife, mattock","count":62,"share":0.08},{"strong":"H4421","lemma":"מִלְחָמָה","xlit":"milchâmâh","gloss":"a battle","kjv":"battle, fight, war","count":56,"share":0.07},{"strong":"H341","lemma":"אֹיֵב","xlit":"ʼôyêb","gloss":"hating","kjv":"enemy, foe","count":39,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","xlit":"Yᵉhôwshûwaʻ","gloss":"Jehoshua , the Jewish leader","kjv":"Jehoshua, Jehoshuah, Joshua","count":35,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H5307","lemma":"נָפַל","xlit":"nâphal","gloss":"to fall, in a great variety of applications","kjv":"be accepted, cast, out), cease","count":35,"share":0.05},{"strong":"H2763","lemma":"חָרַם","xlit":"châram","gloss":"to seclude","kjv":"make accursed, consecrate, destroy, devote","count